          ":question/problem": "$\\int {y}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(${{field-1}}\n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-3\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t=-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}+1)+K.\n$$\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{\u2032}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2t}-\\frac{3t}{{t}^{2}+1})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-3\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}+1)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\sqrt{t})-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}}}\\right)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\sqrt{\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}}})+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
